=86=92 derived =E2=86=92 export architecture</li>
<li><strong>pow-physical</strong>: repair, sensors, actuators, parts, resal=
e =E2=80=94 full SQL schema + source manifests + transforms</li>
<li><strong>pow-uk</strong>: occupations, skills, apprenticeships, tenders,=
 local labour capacity =E2=80=94 full schemas</li>
<li><strong>pow-grid</strong>: Elexon/NESO/DNO capacity, headroom, constrai=
nts =E2=80=94 full schemas</li>
<li><strong>pow-capital</strong>: security master, company exposure, FCA di=
sclosures, IBKR L2, market-assimilation schema</li>
<li><strong>pow-frontier</strong>: papers/GitHub/patents =E2=86=92 typed Se=
esaw hypotheses</li>
<li>cross-system entity/edge/event contracts</li>
<li>causal-latency backtest design</li>
<li>collection urgency vs backfill priority matrix</li>
<li>Jev decision specs</li>
<li>release gates and collector checklists</li>
<li>current source notes and licensing/rights flags</li>
</ul>
<p>Key implementation decision:<br>
<strong>each garden owns its collectors, raw data, normalized tables, trans=
forms, keys and MCP surface. Cross-garden intelligence only joins versioned=
 exported entities/observations/events/relationships.</strong></p>
<p>Priority:</p>
<ol>
<li>build pow-physical</li>
<li>build pow-uk</li>
<li>build pow-grid</li>
<li>build pow-capital fully later, but start a small UK L2 recorder immedia=
tely because book history is ephemeral</li>
<li>keep pow-frontier thin and hypothesis-oriented</li>
<li>keep existing /powpowpow running as system 0.</li>
</ol>

